{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"grep 'CA_EVENT' ../logs/09941e2a9e084150bd1c84ff412dd312/stdout.log; cat ../direct-checks/2854ece9034643948355b1c57a8553d1/omnipaxos_runtime/tests/assurance_generated.rs; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('../direct-checks/2854ece9034643948355b1c57a8553d1/plan.json'));p['harness'].pop('source');print(json.dumps(p,indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"description\": \"Check claim-stream-order with a real five-entry decided history, snapshot of original positions [0,3), and subscription from zero. Observe initial catch-up and a fixed 250ms continuation window; compare the original-log ranks of all emitted retained Decided entries.\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-stream-order\",\n  \"binding_ids\": [\n    \"bind-stream-push\"\n  ],\n  \"harness\": {\n    \"execution_package\": \"./omnipaxos_runtime\",\n    \"files\": {},\n    \"kind\": \"rust_test\",\n    \"description\": \"Build a real three-node cluster, decide five unique values, read their original order, and snapshot the first three entries through the public API. Move the snapshotted core into the actor and subscribe from zero with capacity 32. Consume initial catch-up and every following item until a fixed time cutoff, then verify the underlying retained decided suffix remains unchanged. Compute order from the independently observed original positions, not payload magnitude.\",\n    \"semantic_changes\": [\n      \"No target modifications or injected protocol/storage state.\",\n      \"Test Entry has a snapshot that stores and concatenates the represented prefix values.\",\n      \"Public AsyncRuntime hooks use real Tokio spawn and timers.\"\n    ],\n    \"prerequisites\": [\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"admission\",\n        \"event\": \"subscribed\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"history_ready\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": true,\n            \"reference\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"from\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": 0,\n            \"reference\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"compacted\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": 3,\n            \"reference\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"decided\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": 5,\n            \"reference\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"retained_count\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": 2,\n            \"reference\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"legality\": {\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"src-build\",\n        \"src-memory\",\n        \"src-public-manual-leader\",\n        \"src-leader\",\n        \"src-follower\",\n        \"src-snapshot-api\",\n        \"src-compaction\",\n        \"src-snapshot-producer\",\n        \"src-read\",\n        \"src-runtime-spawn\",\n        \"src-runtime-trait\",\n        \"src-runtime-loop\",\n        \"src-subscriber-push\"\n      ],\n      \"expectation_ids\": [\n        \"src-subscription-contract\",\n        \"doc-log\"\n      ],\n      \"binding_ids\": [],\n      \"derivation\": \"Three fresh valid nodes form leadership through actual protocol messages. Every appended value is decided on all peers before local snapshot(3,true). The snapshot trait stores the actual prefix; subsequent public reads confirm a summary at boundary 3 followed by the two retained entries. No actor API promises an empty initial log: spawn_actor accepts the live core and initializes its cursors from its current metadata. SubscribeDecided is processed before the following same-command-channel barrier. Core safety prefix work occurs before actor startup; actor ticking and event/network drains are active throughout subscription observation.\",\n      \"applicability\": \"One subscription below subscriber/channel capacity; no dropped network traffic, leadership transition, further append, compaction, restart or storage failure during observation. Unique original values are verified, and their observed positions provide a stable order oracle.\",\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"Finite output observation establishes order only for the completed window; no inference of unbounded progress or deadline compliance.\"\n      ],\n      \"conflicts\": [],\n      \"alternatives\": []\n    }\n  },\n  \"monitors\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"monitor-stream-order\",\n      \"checker_id\": \"stream-order\",\n      \"event\": \"stream_window\",\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"bind-stream-push\"\n      ],\n      \"grounding\": {\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"src-subscriber-push\",\n          \"src-read\",\n          \"src-read-classify\",\n          \"src-runtime-loop\"\n        ],\n        \"expectation_ids\": [\n          \"src-subscription-contract\",\n          \"test-stream-order\"\n        ],\n        \"binding_ids\": [\n          \"bind-stream-push\"\n        ],\n        \"derivation\": \"The same subscription receiver supplies every observed item. Retained Decided payloads are mapped to their unique positions in a separately read decided log before compaction. order_preserved is the conjunction of nondecreasing adjacent positions, ignoring snapshot markers; equality is allowed, so the predicate does not strengthen log order to exactly-once delivery. The fixed cutoff is independent of the predicate. Final public read confirms the underlying retained log is stable.\",\n        \"applicability\": \"Only a completed observation window after declared legal snapshot/subscription prerequisites supplies a result. Missing catch-up, unknown entry correlation or premature stream closure is incomplete.\",\n        \"unresolved\": [\n          \"No completion of the unbounded stream is claimed; the result is a safety comparison over the observed finite prefix.\"\n        ],\n        \"conflicts\": [],\n        \"alternatives\": []\n      },\n      \"applicability_conditions\": [],\n      \"admission_alias\": \"admission\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"observable_properties\": [\n    {\n      \"checker_id\": \"stream-order\",\n      \"kind\": \"event_assertion\",\n      \"trigger\": {\n        \"field\": \"event\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": \"stream_window\",\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"assertion\": {\n        \"field\": \"order_preserved\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": true,\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"antecedent\": null,\n      \"identity_fields\": [\n        \"subscription\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Observed retained Decided entries in one stream must not reverse original log positions. Snapshot-marker count is not compared to original log extent.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"uncertainties\": [\n    \"A bounded prefix with no reversal would not settle all possible future schedules.\",\n    \"No claim about duplicate markers, missing compacted values or stream liveness.\",\n    \"The requirement concerns consumption order, not agreement among replica logs.\"\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The stream emitted retained entries in original log-position order `[3, 4, 3, 4]`; the underlying decided suffix stayed unchanged. The `4 → 3` transition violates the documented log-order guarantee. The check allows repeated positions and ignores snapshot markers, so this result does not depend on assuming exactly-once delivery or treating a snapshot as an ordinary entry.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns={'action':'review','artifact_id':'e3801ded979a4d4a851b24b59eb9f2eb','rationale':'Review fixed stream check v1 and trusted execution 09941e2a9e084150bd1c84ff412dd312. Its completed output contains an actual reversal among retained decided positions, independently of snapshot-marker semantics.','review_items':[{'aspect':'checker_correspondence','status':'no_issue_found','source_ids':['src-subscription-contract','test-stream-order','src-subscriber-push','src-runtime-loop','src-runtime-spawn','src-runtime-trait','src-runtime-tokio-adapter','src-build','src-memory','src-leader','src-follower','src-read','src-read-classify','src-snapshot-api','src-compaction','src-snapshot-producer'],'rationale':'The accepted claim-stream-order v1 follows the public subscribe_decided contract: backlog and later LogEntry output must be in log order. The selected oracle only forbids a decrease in original position among retained Decided entries. It allows equal positions and ignores snapshot markers, so it does not invent an exactly-once contract or demand recovery of compacted individual entries.\\\\n\\\\nThe fixed harness establishes a valid three-node configuration and generates every protocol message through actual core instances. It uses public manual leadership, appends five unique values, and requires all replicas to report decided extent 5 before compaction. A public precompaction read records original history [81,23,67,42,19]. snapshot(Some(3),true) executes the real compaction producer with a prefix-preserving Snapshot implementation; reads confirm summary boundary 3 followed by retained values 42 and 19. The original actor core is moved into spawn_actor with no storage replacement or private mutation. The public constructor does not require empty history. The sole subscription is below configured capacity, its command precedes a same-channel read barrier, and the receiver is actively drained. Events and outgoing transport are also drained; ordinary real Tokio timers drive the actor.\\\\n\\\\nExecution 09941e2a9e084150bd1c84ff412dd312 records the declared admission for subscription from-zero with from=0, compacted=3, decided=5 and two retained entries. It then records a snapshot marker followed by Decided values 42,19,42,19, at independently recovered positions 3,4,3,4. The completed stream_window event has order_preserved=false and observed_items=5. Final live actor reads verify the stable retained suffix is still [42,19] at extent 5. No additional appends, reconfiguration, recovery, leadership changes or compaction occur during the observation. This is one legal history with the actual compaction producer, actual cursor consumer and actual subscriber endpoint.\\\\n\\\\nThe operation identity is the unique subscription label, independent of payloads and the compared order result. Each Decided payload is mapped to its unique rank in the separately observed original log; deliberately nonmonotonic payload numbers prevent confusing numeric value order with log order. The source computes order_preserved by checking adjacent ranks for nondecrease. Raw per-item events independently show the decisive 4-to-3 decrease. The result is not predetermined by the input or selected by an observed failure. Initial catch-up values are observed rather than asserted to match the expected stream order; the observation ends at a fixed elapsed-time cutoff regardless of reversal.\\\\n\\\\nThe implementation explanation is conditional and matches this prefix. Initial push_to_sub successfully emits three representations: one snapshot and two retained entries. Its cursor increments from 0 to 3 rather than advancing to original extent 5. A later push_to_all_subs therefore reads original positions 3 and 4 again and appends them after the already delivered position 4. Ordinary noncompacted reads do not exhibit this representation/position mismatch. Channel-full and closure branches do not explain the witness: capacity is 32 and only five observed items are emitted to an actively drained receiver. The finite window is sufficient for a positive safety counterexample; no deadline failure or infinite-stall conclusion is inferred. The process completed and all result data exists; process PASS alone is not the evidence.','counterevidence':[],'limitations':['Only one precompacted, stable-log subscription history is established; multiple-subscriber interactions and compaction after subscription are separate.','A 250ms window does not establish future progress or completeness of an unbounded stream, but the observed backward transition remains a complete safety witness.','The underlying decided suffix remains stable; no consensus disagreement is observed.','No assertion is made about exactly-once marker delivery or reconstructing compacted individual entries.'],'report_title':'快照前缀导致决定日志订阅回退到已发送的位置','report_answer':'从已压缩前缀开始订阅时，实际保留条目的位置序列为 3、4、3、4，而底层决定日志未变化。订阅游标把一个快照摘要计为一个原始日志位置，后续推送重发旧后缀，产生 4→3 的顺序回退。'}],'feedback':{'ref_ids':['a672385fe7194098a189c850a5f210c8','b-subscriber','f-sub-cursor','e3801ded979a4d4a851b24b59eb9f2eb','09941e2a9e084150bd1c84ff412dd312','src-subscriber-push','src-read'],'answered':'The legal snapshot/subscription history produced retained-entry ranks [3,4,3,4], including a backward transition while the original decided suffix remained stable. Cursor counting of compacted representations explains the repeated suffix across initial and periodic push paths.','remaining':['Multiple-subscriber and post-subscription compaction consequences remain independent.','Core delayed same-ballot synchronization and heartbeat eligibility questions remain open.'],'understanding':'updated','rationale':'The current execution answers the selected reversal question. Replace its answered unknown with the sourced representation/position relationship at the next map-bearing handoff; do not transfer this result to liveness or consensus agreement.'}}\njson.dump(s,open('submission-07.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-04_18-47-07-omnipaxos-real-run --submission submission-07.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
